sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant PC as PipelineConfig.jsx / Runner.jsx
    participant CI as ciPipeline.js
    participant DB as Database (Postgres)
    participant S3 as S3 (resultsStore.js)
    participant GP as Git Platform (GitHub/GitLab/Bitbucket)
    participant CIP as CI Runner<br/>(GitHub Actions / GitLab CI / Bitbucket Pipelines)
    participant Target as Target Application

    rect rgb(255, 245, 200)
    Note over User,CIP: Setup - configure external CI provider
    User->>PC: Configure CI provider (repo, branch, trigger token/PAT)
    PC->>CI: POST /api/projects/:id/ci/config
    CI->>DB: INSERT/UPDATE ci_pipeline_configs

    User->>PC: Generate CI YAML file
    PC->>CI: POST /api/projects/:id/ci/generate-yaml
    CI->>DB: Fetch test suite(s) to get script paths
    CI->>CI: Build .github/workflows/*.yml or .gitlab-ci.yml or bitbucket-pipelines.yml<br/>(includes a JTL validation step: exit 1 on 0 requests or 100% error rate)
    CI->>GP: Commit + push generated workflow file
    end

    rect rgb(210, 235, 255)
    Note over User,CIP: Runtime - trigger and execute (JMeter/K6 run on the CI runner, NOT the Peako server)
    User->>PC: Click "Run via CI"
    PC->>CI: POST /api/projects/:id/ci/trigger
    CI->>GP: Push generated script to workspace repo
    CI->>GP: Dispatch workflow_dispatch / pipeline trigger / pipeline API call
    CI->>DB: INSERT ci_pipeline_runs (status pending)
    GP->>CIP: Runner picks up the job
    CIP->>Target: jmeter -n -t script.jmx  /  k6 run script.js
    CIP->>CIP: Validate JTL — exit 1 immediately on 0 requests or 100% error rate
    CIP->>GP: Upload results.jtl + HTML report as CI artifact
    end

    rect rgb(220, 250, 220)
    Note over User,CIP: Result sync - Peako pulls artifacts back
    PC->>CI: Poll GET /ci/runs/:runId/status
    CI->>GP: Check run/job status via provider API
    CI->>GP: Download artifact zip
    CI->>S3: writeZipEntries() - JTL + report, zero local disk
    CI->>CI: evaluateRules() against project rules
    CI->>DB: UPDATE ci_pipeline_runs / execution_runs SET status
    CI->>CI: sendAlertEmail (pipeline summary)
    CI-->>PC: Status: completed / failed

    alt run failed
        CI->>CI: autoHealer.js diagnoseWithAi() - 1 automatic attempt
        CI->>GP: Push fixed script
        CI->>CIP: Re-trigger CI job
        Note over User,CIP: Additional attempts require manual "Heal Again" with a steering instruction
    end
    end
